<title>Exam 2</title>

<introduction>
<p>
Exam 2 of this quarter (Fall 2026), with solutions. These were the
instructions on the exam:
</p>

<p>
<ul>
<li><p>You have <alert>65 minutes</alert>. The exam has 7 problems and is worth <alert>20 points</alert>.</p></li>
<li><p>This is a closed-book exam. No aids of your own are permitted: no formula sheets, notes, phones, tablets, smart watches, or similar. <alert>Calculators of any kind are not permitted.</alert></p></li>
<li><p>Write your work in a neat and organized format and <alert>fully justify every step</alert>. An answer without supporting work may receive little or no credit.</p></li>
<li><p>Give exact answers. Decimal approximations are not required.</p></li>
<li><p>If you need more room, use the blank page at the end of the booklet and say so on the page of the problem.</p></li>
<li><p>Any violation of academic integrity, such as the use of AI, calculators, etc., may result in receiving an F and being reported to the Office of Student Life.</p></li>
</ul>
</p>

<p>
The solutions below are fuller than what is expected on the exam. The items
marked <q>check</q> are sanity checks, not required steps.
